Hi, if you are using the tidyLPA::estimate_profiles() function, it uses the mclust package on the backend. It works by first performing hierarchical cluster analysis to provide starting values for the expectation-maximization algorithm. Unfortunately, in the present version on CRAN, we don’t provide functionality to change the convergence criterion and the maximum number of iterations, though I believe you an do so through the mclust::emControl() function (which is passed to the mclust::mclust() function; see here: https://rdrr.io/cran/mclust/man/emControl.html

Hope this helps,

Josh

